Package: datareuseR
Type: Package
Title: Teaching Open Data Reuse with Library Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Data sets and helper functions for learning to reuse open
    public-sector data in library and information science courses. It
    includes a practice file of library loans with typical quality problems,
    a dated copy of the Madrid municipal libraries directory, and functions
    to read open data files with unknown encoding and separator, measure
    completeness, check the five-star open data scheme and FAIR criteria,
    combine licence obligations, estimate the break-even point of a
    freemium data service, and query the Spanish national open data
    catalogue (datos.gob.es) with an offline fallback. It accompanies the
    open textbook "Reutilización de datos abiertos y documentos"
    <doi:10.5281/zenodo.24500934>. Messages and documentation are in Spanish.
